  "notes": "Modified cash basis village; governmental = General, Street, Fire and Ambulance and Other Governmental funds (Total Governmental Funds column, pp5-6); business-type = Water and Sewer (p8 Total column). Roll-forward: 424,030 + 552,306 - 638,080 + 148,456 - 148,456 = 338,256; transfers are fund-column sums (Total column blank). Business-type: 553,745 + 165,288 - 117,468 = 601,565. County treasurer revenues 235,863 split using the Statement of Activities general revenues (p3: property taxes 183,248, motor vehicle taxes 14,517; remainder 38,098 is inside p3 Intergovernmental sources). Balance sheet (user 2026-10-27): governmental lines from the governmental funds statement (p4, totals equal p1); business-type from p1. Detail (user 2026-10-27): the budget schedule (p9) is a combined all-funds schedule, so per-fund statement columns are used for General, Street, Fire and Ambulance (p5-6), Water and Sewer (p8); the nonmajor funds use their combining schedule (p10, 9 funds, Total column). County Treasurer schedule (p11) not recorded in detail: the same money is in the County treasurer revenues lines. Read pages 1-11 of 11"
